{
  "_comment": [
    "The condition contract, read by BOTH sides:",
    "  pkg/infra/evaluator/condition_number_shape_test.go  (EvaluateConditions)",
    "  ui/src/__tests__/matchesConditionParity.test.ts     (matchesCondition)",
    "",
    "It lives in one file because the previous arrangement was two hand-kept",
    "tables, one 'transcribed' from the other. That catches a TypeScript",
    "regression against a frozen snapshot of Go; it does not catch the Go side",
    "changing, because nothing makes the transcription fail when the original",
    "moves. Adding an operator in Go left the editor asserting the old truth,",
    "green, while the twins had actually drifted.",
    "",
    "JSON is the right medium and not an accident: every read path normalises a",
    "field through a JSON round trip, so the values here arrive at both",
    "implementations the way a real message's would.",
    "",
    "Adding a case is one edit and both languages run it."
  ],

  "operators": {
    "_comment": [
      "Every operator the editor offers, each with a field and value that make",
      "it TRUE -- so a blanket `return false` cannot pass -- plus negations that",
      "must be FALSE, so a blanket `return true` cannot either.",
      "The second group are aliases: stored configs and the API use them."
    ],
    "matching": [
      { "operator": "=",            "field": "abc", "value": "abc" },
      { "operator": "!=",           "field": "abc", "value": "zzz" },
      { "operator": ">",            "field": 10,    "value": "5"   },
      { "operator": ">=",           "field": 10,    "value": "5"   },
      { "operator": "<",            "field": 5,     "value": "10"  },
      { "operator": "<=",           "field": 5,     "value": "10"  },
      { "operator": "contains",     "field": "abc", "value": "b"   },
      { "operator": "not_contains", "field": "abc", "value": "zzz" },
      { "operator": "regex",        "field": "abc", "value": "^a"  },
      { "operator": "not_regex",    "field": "abc", "value": "zzz" },
      { "operator": "eq",           "field": "abc", "value": "abc" },
      { "operator": "neq",          "field": "abc", "value": "zzz" },
      { "operator": "gt",           "field": 10,    "value": "5"   },
      { "operator": "gte",          "field": 10,    "value": "5"   },
      { "operator": "lt",           "field": 5,     "value": "10"  },
      { "operator": "lte",          "field": 5,     "value": "10"  }
    ],
    "notMatching": [
      { "operator": "not_contains", "field": "abc", "value": "b"   },
      { "operator": "not_regex",    "field": "abc", "value": "^a"  },
      { "operator": "neq",          "field": "abc", "value": "abc" }
    ]
  },

  "numericEquality": {
    "_comment": [
      "`=` on a number is numeric, so the spelling of the value does not matter;",
      "on a string it stays string equality, so an id does not lose its zeros.",
      "`!=` must be the exact negation of each, or a config can satisfy both."
    ],
    "cases": [
      { "name": "same number, trailing zero",        "field": 100,     "value": "100.00", "equal": true  },
      { "name": "same number, decimal zero",         "field": 100.5,   "value": "100.50", "equal": true  },
      { "name": "same number, leading zero",         "field": 100,     "value": "0100",   "equal": true  },
      { "name": "same number, plus sign",            "field": 100,     "value": "+100",   "equal": true  },
      { "name": "same number, exponent",             "field": 100,     "value": "1e2",    "equal": true  },
      { "name": "same text",                         "field": 100,     "value": "100",    "equal": true  },
      { "name": "different number",                  "field": 100,     "value": "101",    "equal": false },
      { "name": "not a number",                      "field": 100,     "value": "abc",    "equal": false },
      { "name": "string field keeps string equality","field": "007",   "value": "7",      "equal": false },
      { "name": "string field exact still matches",  "field": "007",   "value": "007",    "equal": true  },
      { "name": "string field numeric text",         "field": "100.0", "value": "100.00", "equal": false },
      { "name": "bool field is not a number",        "field": true,    "value": "1",      "equal": false },
      { "name": "empty value is not zero",           "field": 0,       "value": "",       "equal": false }
    ]
  },

  "wideInteger": {
    "_comment": [
      "A number normalises to float64 on every read path, and the string a",
      "condition compares against has to be the string the user was shown.",
      "Rendering it with Go's %v put 1704207845 on screen as 1.704207845e+09",
      "while the wire, the browser and the editor's simulator all said the",
      "digits. Nothing below 1e6 drifted, so ids and timestamps broke and the",
      "test data did not."
    ],
    "field": 1704207845,
    "cases": [
      {
            "operator": "=",
            "value": "1704207845",
            "expected": true
      },
      {
            "operator": "=",
            "value": "1704207846",
            "expected": false
      },
      {
            "operator": "!=",
            "value": "1704207845",
            "expected": false
      },
      {
            "operator": "!=",
            "value": "1704207846",
            "expected": true
      },
      {
            "operator": "contains",
            "value": "042078",
            "expected": true
      },
      {
            "operator": "contains",
            "value": "e+09",
            "expected": false
      },
      {
            "operator": "not_contains",
            "value": "042078",
            "expected": false
      },
      {
            "operator": "regex",
            "value": "^1704",
            "expected": true
      },
      {
            "operator": "regex",
            "value": "^\\d+$",
            "expected": true
      },
      {
            "operator": "not_regex",
            "value": "^1704",
            "expected": false
      },
      {
            "operator": ">",
            "value": "1704207844",
            "expected": true
      },
      {
            "operator": "<",
            "value": "1704207846",
            "expected": true
      }
]
  }
}
